IoC (Inversion of Control) --> 
A Spring Container that controls creating and managing objects.
//Student student = context.getBean(Student.class);
here, Spring creates the object --> Student student = new Student();

--> Objects created are stored inside the IoC Container.
--> IoC and DI are not the same.
--> IoC Container stores objects, not code.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependency Injection (DI) -->
A technique where Spring provides the required object (dependency) to another object and injects it automatically.
here the required object is called dependency.

Code Example :
Course.java -->

package com.example;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class Course 
{
    public void learn() 
    {
        System.out.println("Learning Spring");
    }
}

Student.java -->

package com.example;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class Student 
{
    @Autowired
    private Course spring;

    public void study() 
    {
        spring.learn();
    }
}

Main.java -->

package com.example;

import org.springframework.context.ApplicationContext;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.AnnotationConfigApplicationContext;

public class Main 
{
    public static void main(String[] args) 
    {
        ApplicationContext context = new AnnotationConfigApplicationContext("com.example");
        Student student = context.getBean(Student.class);
        student.study();
    }
}

Explanation :
@Autowired --> Automatically inject the Course object here.
private Course course; and not public Course course; is Because of Encapsulation, so only Students can access 

IoC vs DI :
| IoC                     | DI                            |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Principle               | Technique                     |
| Control given to Spring | Dependency supplied by Spring |
| Bigger concept          | Part of IoC                   |
--> Spring IoC Container injects dependencies
